  Context: [38;5;153mindex.html[39m is a bare static page — no framework, no build step, no tests, and [38;5;153m<main>[39m is empty. That raises
  the one question that actually matters.

  [1mThe fork:[0m you said the checkbox lets users mark [3mitems[0m done, but there are no items on the page yet. So either I add
  just the checkbox control itself and you wire it to items later, or I render it as part of a task row so it's visibly
  doing its job.

  - [1mCheckbox only[0m — smallest change, one [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m in [38;5;153m<main>[39m. Costs: it sits there unlabeled with nothing
    to mark. Cheap to extend later.
  - [1mCheckbox + a task row[0m — a labeled checkbox representing one task item, with a "done" visual state. Slightly more
    markup/CSS, but it's a component you can duplicate per item. Also cheap to change.

  I'd recommend the second: same effort, and an unlabeled bare checkbox is an accessibility dead end you'd have to redo
  anyway.
